Shepr change log. Newest first.
Every outside contribution is listed with the contributor's GitHub profile and, when one could be verified, their X profile.

2026-10-12  v42 (1b97a6d)  HANCORE  https://github.com/HANCORE-linux
  X: https://x.com/hancore_linux (listed on their GitHub profile, checked 2026-10-13)
  Review of the Omarchy plugin for the marketplace (omacom/omarchy-plugin-marketplace#11176): the one-time pairing code
  was passed to qrencode as an argument, where `ps` could show it, and the QR picture could fall back to /tmp with default
  permissions. Fixed in 1b97a6d: the code goes over stdin, the picture is born 0600 in a private directory the CLI checks
  first, never /tmp, and Cancel removes it. v43 also removes it when `shepr pair` finishes waiting.

2026-10-10  v38  Jordan Partridge  https://github.com/jordanpartridge
  X: none found (checked 2026-10-10: GitHub lists no X account, only LinkedIn, and his site links none)
  #1  A session herdr no longer has is left, not polled. herdr answers agent_not_found, Shepr used to turn that into HTTP 400,
      and the phone asked again every 6 seconds. It now gets a 404, closes the session back to the queue and says "That session is gone."
  #2  `shepr pair` names the systemd unit installed on this machine. It reads ~/.config/systemd/user and names the unit that runs
      this server.py (symlinks included); with none installed it names both install styles instead of ordering one.
  #3  The install block in the README links `shepr` into whichever of ~/.local/bin or ~/bin your PATH already searches first,
      and falls back to ~/.local/bin, so `shepr pair` is found on the first try.
